# Beartropy Alert System - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This project uses **Beartropy Alert System**, a multi-channel alerting package for Laravel.

## Sending Alerts

```php
use Beartropy\AlertSystem\Facades\Alert;

Alert::send('alert_type', 'Message text', ['key' => 'value'], ['mailSubject' => 'Subject']);
```

## Channels
- **Mail**: Standard Laravel Mailable
- **Telegram**: Bot API with chat ID
- **Discord**: Webhook URL

## Management Components
```blade
@livewire('alert-system.manage-types')
@livewire('alert-system.manage-channels')
@livewire('alert-system.manage-recipients')
@livewire('alert-system.manage-logs')
```

## Best Practices
- Create alert types for each category: "server_error", "payment_failed", "user_registered"
- Use cooldown to prevent alert storms: `config('alert-system.cooldown_minutes')`
- Set `envs` to prevent accidental alerts in development
- Pass structured `$details` array for rich alert content
- Use `mailSubject` option for meaningful email subjects
